{"coverage_warning":"Only 2 complete measured days exist and they cover VM-local Claude Code CLI sessions only; Muse chat/cron tokens and the Mac Foreman are NOT metered. Note 2026-11-02 alone (1811445 new units) is about 127% of this cap (1422170), so stop verdicts are expected on heavy delegation days until more history accrues or the cap is re-derived. Re-derive from the rolling average rather than guessing.","daily_cap_units":1422170,"derivation":"Unit correction applied 2026-11-03 (approved by the operator): cache writes are now weighted by TTL -- ephemeral_1h x2.0, ephemeral_5m x1.25, unsplit writes x1.25 fallback (split parsed via cache_caller_report.py; fallback count at correction: 0 records) -- instead of the original flat x1.25, which priced every write at the 5-minute rate while the measured mix on this VM was 1h 100% / 5m 0% (705814 cache-creation tokens, 2026-11-01..03), understating the write component by about 37%. Other weights unchanged: input x1, cache read x0.1, output x5. Day values below are rounded as the governor reports them. OLD unit (write x1.25 flat): 2026-11-01 = 53424 units, 2026-11-02 = 1423319 units, mean = 738371.5, old cap = 1107557. NEW unit: 2026-11-01 = 84782 units, 2026-11-02 = 1811445 units, mean = 948113.5. Cap re-derived under the same rule (baseline daily average x 1.5), NOT carried over from the old unit: 948113.5 x 1.5 = 1422170 units (rounded). Source data: usage_report.py / cache_caller_report.py over local Claude Code CLI logs (the two parsers reconcile exactly per day).","rule":"trial cap = baseline daily average x 1.5 (the operator's direction, 2026-11-03)","set_on":"2026-11-03","unit":"weighted units: input x1, cache read x0.1, output x5, cache write ephemeral_1h x2.0 / ephemeral_5m x1.25 (unsplit x1.25 fallback); TTL split added 2026-11-03, replacing flat write x1.25","warn_fraction":0.8}